                    {
                        "form_id": "8d4f430a-9b65-40eb-a963-3b67d30a7dd7",
                        "entry_id": "486878a3-29f4-3ac6-ba01-f9eb1327f8cd",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "профана́циях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5fec0424-eda4-3c77-ad74-32a031d232eb",
                        "entry_id": "486878a3-29f4-3ac6-ba01-f9eb1327f8cd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. искажение чего-либо невежеством, оскорбительным обращением, отношением; опошление, осквернение, кощунство"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb34a244-c4f9-4be4-942d-7e794f3a2158",
                                "sense_id": "5fec0424-eda4-3c77-ad74-32a031d232eb",
                                "text": "Вот против этих-то братских «исповедей» и восставали противники старчества, говоря, что это профанация исповеди как таинства, почти кощунство, хотя тут было совсем иное."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5ce1aae-186b-44ea-8a04-a17eb6994b41",
                                "sense_id": "5fec0424-eda4-3c77-ad74-32a031d232eb",
                                "text": "— Я рассказываю о ней, об этой дивной женщине, а вы — горничная! Это — профанация! У вас, видно, горничные только на уме…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e4c242f9-e248-49cc-b092-381a120e0796",
                        "source_entry_id": "486878a3-29f4-3ac6-ba01-f9eb1327f8cd",
                        "source_sense_id": "5fec0424-eda4-3c77-ad74-32a031d232eb",
                        "target_lang_word": "profanity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "profanity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "face2857-582c-3060-97bd-ea11491d0358",
                                        "entry_id": "d9ed9e0d-ba26-3f71-bde8-5f4591733e77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being profane; quality of irreverence, of treating sacred things with contempt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76cc6980-832c-4b2a-9c39-41edab25fe0f",
                                                "sense_id": "face2857-582c-3060-97bd-ea11491d0358",
                                                "text": "The overwhelming power of his imagination led him to contemplate acts of impiety and profanity, and to a vivid realisation of the dangers these involved."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "012545b2-d338-3302-8e15-955b37b12694",
                                        "entry_id": "d9ed9e0d-ba26-3f71-bde8-5f4591733e77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Obscene, lewd or abusive language."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d58ebb08-808f-4bcb-b845-8808958c475f",
                                                "sense_id": "012545b2-d338-3302-8e15-955b37b12694",
                                                "text": "He ran up and down the street screaming profanities like a madman."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a827943-b340-4869-bad1-a5b489d2ea41",
                                                "sense_id": "012545b2-d338-3302-8e15-955b37b12694",
                                                "text": "Swearing doesn't just mean what we now understand by \"dirty words\". It is entwined, in social and linguistic history, with the other sort of swearing: vows and oaths. Consider for a moment the origins of almost any word we have for bad language – \"profanity\", \"curses\", \"oaths\" and \"swearing\" itself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
